 Good changes! A few issues to fix:

## 1. Bad Import
```javascript
import { update } from 'tab.module.js'; // Remove - not used
```

## 2. Missing Async/Await
```javascript
export const initialize = async (rt) => { // Add async
	runtime = rt;
	await registerProviders(); // Add await  
	setConfigOptions();
};

const registerProviders = async () => // Add async - you're calling runtime methods
```

## 3. Config Update Issue
The config options are set once at initialization, but they need to update when provider selection changes. Add a config change listener:

```javascript
export const initialize = async (rt) => {
	runtime = rt;
	await registerProviders();
	setConfigOptions();
	setupConfigListener();
};

const setupConfigListener = () => {
	// Watch for provider changes to update model options
	let lastProvider = config.provider;
	setInterval(() => {
		if (config.provider !== lastProvider) {
			lastProvider = config.provider;
			setModelConfigOptions();
		}
	}, 1000);
};
```

## 4. Inconsistent Property Access
```javascript
// Pick one style:
manifest.config.model.options = ... // Direct
// OR
manifest.config.model["options"] = ... // Bracket (you mixed both)
```

## 5. Override Parameters
Nice addition allowing `provider`/`model` override in `prompt()` params! That's flexible.

## 6. Error Handling
Consider logging when no providers found:
```javascript
const registerProviders = async () => {
	providers = runtime.getModulesWithProperty('inferenceModels').filter(p => ['makeRequest', 'getContent'].every(fn => typeof p[fn] === 'function'));
	runtime.log(`[Inference] Registered ${providers.length} providers`);
};
```

Otherwise excellent compression and clean separation of concerns!

